# Template for the local development stack. Copy it and edit:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   docker compose up --build
#
# Compose reads `.env` automatically; every value below already has the same
# default baked into docker-compose.yml, so the stack runs with no .env at
# all. This file exists to make the knobs discoverable — and to give
# RELAIX_PUBLIC_URL a value a real handset can actually dial.

# --- What the QR code tells a phone to dial -------------------------------
# The one value most people need to change. `localhost` means the *phone*
# to a handset, so the default (host.docker.internal) is useless to it.
#
#   phone over USB   grpc://127.0.0.1:9090   with the two adb reverse below
#   emulator (AVD)   grpc://10.0.2.2:9090    10.0.2.2 is the host from an AVD
#   phone over Wi-Fi grpc://<PC LAN IP>:9090 needs a firewall rule for 8080/9090
#
# For USB, run once per cable plug — the tunnels drop when adb restarts:
#   adb reverse tcp:9090 tcp:9090 && adb reverse tcp:8080 tcp:8080
#
# Use grpcs:// instead of grpc:// once the gRPC listener has a certificate
# (RELAIX_TLS_CERT / RELAIX_TLS_KEY); the agent refuses to guess and will
# dial exactly the scheme it is given.
RELAIX_PUBLIC_URL=grpc://127.0.0.1:9090

# --- Secrets --------------------------------------------------------------
# Replace all three before this runs anywhere that is not a laptop.
# RELAIX_API_KEY guards the REST API; RELAIX_CALLBACK_SECRET signs the
# outgoing status webhooks (HMAC), so changing it invalidates signatures
# receivers may already be verifying.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
RELAIX_API_KEY=change-me
RELAIX_CALLBACK_SECRET=change-me

# --- Ports ----------------------------------------------------------------
# 5432 is the right default but collides with a locally installed Postgres.
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
HTTP_PORT=8080
GRPC_PORT=9090

# --- Build and logging ----------------------------------------------------
# VERSION is stamped into the gatewayd binary. RELAIX_LOG_LEVEL=debug logs
# every gRPC message, which is what you want while bringing up an agent.
VERSION=dev
RELAIX_LOG_LEVEL=info
